  "toolCallCount": 0,
  "toolCalls": [],
  "finalAnswer": "For general medical education, signs of anaphylaxis are often categorized by the systems they affect, including the respiratory and cardiovascular systems.\n\nHere are examples of warning signs that can affect breathing and circulation:\n\n**Breathing signs:**\n*   Throat or tongue swelling\n*   Difficulty breathing\n*   Shortness of breath\n*   Wheezing\n*   Stridor\n*   Throat tightness\n\n**Circulation signs:**\n*   Low blood pressure or hypotension\n*   Weak pulse\n*   Rapid pulse or fast heartbeat\n*   Dizziness\n*   Fainting\n*   Loss of consciousness\n\n**Important note:** These examples are for informational purposes only. Anaphylaxis can manifest in different ways, and other symptoms, such as skin reactions (flushing, hives, itching, or tingling) or digestive issues, may also occur. If you experience any of these symptoms or symptoms that concern you, please consult a medical professional for evaluation.",
